IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`
IMPORT `sgta-tv-ba-schedule`
IMPORT `sgta-tv-seat`

-- QUARANTINED FILE (BRIEF.md "Quarantine"; see TV-QUESTION.md): worked cases for the receiver seat, in PAIRS of days: the day of the CONDUCT first, the day the
-- law is READ AS AT second.  Expected values are written by hand from the texts, with the reasoning in TV-QUESTION.md.
-- Every case is one person who owns a receiver that picks up broadcasts as radio waves (receive only, no decoder), holds no licence of their own, and
-- knows of no regulation or exemption that covers them, unless the case says otherwise.
-- Argument order of the exported questions: day, month, year (conduct); reading day, month, year; the kind of receiver; "only receives"; "picks up by
-- radio waves"; "holds a section 5 licence"; "holds another authorisation"; "has a Minister's exemption"; "holds a treaty licence"; "conforms to
-- published standards"; "localised on-site"; "only in a band the item authorises".
-- Where each kind of receiver stands: the Broadcasting Act's First Schedule lists a television (item 1) and a radio, FM or AM (item 2, "broadcast sound
-- receiver"), in the Revised Editions 2003 and 2012, and S 549/2012 (first published 31 Oct 2012, deemed in operation from 1 Jan 2011) leaves the TVRO
-- system alone; a satellite dish system is listed throughout.  The same conduct therefore has two answers on the two sides of 31 Oct 2012.

§ `Constants`

`the general penalty` MEANS `Penalty` OF 10000, 36, 1000, TRUE
`the penalty before Act 10 of 2005` MEANS `Penalty` OF 10000, 36, 0, TRUE
`an offence under s 54(2)` MEANS JUST (`an offence under` OF "section 54(2)", `the general penalty`)
`an offence under s 55(1)` MEANS JUST (`an offence under` OF "section 55(1)", `the general penalty`)
`an offence under s 54(2) before Act 10 of 2005` MEANS JUST (`an offence under` OF "section 54(2)", `the penalty before Act 10 of 2005`)
`no offence` MEANS JUST `no offence under this provision`

§ `Date (1): conduct on 31 December 2010 and before`

-- Revised Edition 2000 as amended by Act 10 of 2005 (both printed in the Gazette) is the Act's text; the First Schedule (Revised Edition 2003) lists a television and a sound receiver;
-- s 95 Reading A: the Act does not apply to the licensing of listed broadcasting apparatus, so s 54(1)(b) is not contravened.  S 549/2012 is deemed from 1 Jan 2011, not before.
