-- a television in a house or flat: reg 27(1) until 20 Jun 2004, then no prohibition in the regulations
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "reg 27(1): 'No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence' (BA1994-RG1.txt:481-482)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required to operate a broadcast television receiver in a house or flat: S 333/2004 cl 12(a) deletes reg 27(1) and (2) and substitutes a paragraph (1) that says only 'An application for a licence to install or operate a broadcast television receiver may be made at any post office or at such other places as the Authority may require' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:137-144); reg 27(3) remains ('A licence shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers by the licensee, members of his family and domestic servants resident at the address specified therein', BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), reg 27(4), amended by cl 12(b) to say 'installed or operated by', requires a separate licence for a television installed or operated by a lodger, boarder, resident guest or any person occupying a portion of the premises under a separate tenancy (BA1994-RG1.txt:489-493; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:145-146), and reg 7 now speaks of a contravention of 'section 20 (1) of the Act' alone, cl 6 having deleted 'or of regulation 17, 27 or 36' (BA1994-RG1.txt:264-266; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:92-94)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 29 2 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "reg 27(1): 'No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence' (BA1994-RG1.txt:481-482)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 14 6 2004 `television` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "reg 27(1): 'No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence' (BA1994-RG1.txt:481-482)"
-- a television in a vehicle or a vessel: reg 27(1) and reg 28(2), then reg 28(2) alone
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a vehicle` EQUALS "reg 27(1): 'No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence' (BA1994-RG1.txt:481-482); and reg 28(2): 'A separate licence shall be required for every broadcast television receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:501-504)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a vehicle` EQUALS "reg 28(2), which S 333/2004 does not amend (cl 13 amends reg 28(1) and (5)): 'A separate licence shall be required for every broadcast television receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:501-504; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:149-160)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a vessel that has no ship station licence` EQUALS "reg 28(2), which S 333/2004 does not amend (cl 13 amends reg 28(1) and (5)): 'A separate licence shall be required for every broadcast television receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:501-504; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:149-160)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a vessel that has no ship station licence` EQUALS "reg 27(1): 'No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence' (BA1994-RG1.txt:481-482); and reg 28(2): 'A separate licence shall be required for every broadcast television receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:501-504)"
-- a television in a commercial property: reg 27(1) until 20 Jun 2004; reg 29A(1) from 21 Jun 2004
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a commercial property` EQUALS "reg 27(1): 'No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence' (BA1994-RG1.txt:481-482)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a commercial property` EQUALS "reg 29A(1), inserted by S 333/2004 cl 14: 'A separate licence shall be required for every broadcast television receiver installed in a commercial property' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:162-167)"
-- a radio in a vehicle or a vessel: reg 23(1) until 20 Jun 2004; from 21 Jun 2004 reg 23(2) names a vessel only
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `FM radio` `in a vehicle` EQUALS "reg 23(1): 'A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:441-444)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `FM radio` `in a vehicle` EQUALS "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver in a vehicle: S 333/2004 cl 11(a) deletes reg 23(1) and (2) and substitutes a paragraph (1) on where to apply and a paragraph (2) that names a vessel only (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:123-133)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `FM radio` `in a vessel that has no ship station licence` EQUALS "reg 23(1): 'A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:441-444)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `FM radio` `in a vessel that has no ship station licence` EQUALS "reg 23(2), substituted by S 333/2004 cl 11: 'A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:123-133)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `AM radio` `in a vehicle` EQUALS "reg 23(1): 'A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:441-444)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `AM radio` `in a vehicle` EQUALS "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver in a vehicle: S 333/2004 cl 11(a) deletes reg 23(1) and (2) and substitutes a paragraph (1) on where to apply and a paragraph (2) that names a vessel only (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:123-133)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `AM radio` `in a vessel that has no ship station licence` EQUALS "reg 23(1): 'A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-RG1.txt:441-444)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `AM radio` `in a vessel that has no ship station licence` EQUALS "reg 23(2), substituted by S 333/2004 cl 11: 'A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:123-133)"
-- a radio in a house or flat, and in a commercial property
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 29 2 2004 4 11 2026 `FM radio` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "no regulation of the Revised Edition 2004 says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver there; reg 27(3) says a television licence 'shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers' at the address (BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), and item 2 of the First Schedule prices 'Licence for a broadcast sound receiver' at $27 for 12 months (BA1994-RG1.txt:629)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `FM radio` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver there; reg 27(3) says a television licence 'shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers' at the address (BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), and item 2 of the First Schedule, which S 333/2004 does not amend, prices 'Licence for a broadcast sound receiver' at $27 for 12 months (BA1994-RG1.txt:629)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `AM radio` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver there; reg 27(3) says a television licence 'shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers' at the address (BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), and item 2 of the First Schedule, which S 333/2004 does not amend, prices 'Licence for a broadcast sound receiver' at $27 for 12 months (BA1994-RG1.txt:629)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `FM radio` `in a commercial property` EQUALS "no regulation of the Revised Edition 2004 says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver there; reg 27(3) says a television licence 'shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers' at the address (BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), and item 2 of the First Schedule prices 'Licence for a broadcast sound receiver' at $27 for 12 months (BA1994-RG1.txt:629)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `FM radio` `in a commercial property` EQUALS "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver there; reg 29A(2), inserted by S 333/2004, says a licence under reg 29A(1) 'shall permit the use of one or more broadcast sound receivers' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:168-169)"
-- a satellite dish system
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 20 6 2004 4 11 2026 `satellite dish system` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "Rg 1, Revised Edition 2004, reg 2(1): the definition of 'broadcast television receiver' ends 'but does not include any Television Receive-Only Satellite Receiving System' (BA1994-RG1.txt:144-148), so a TVRO system is outside the 'broadcast television receiver' of reg 27(1)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 21 6 2004 4 11 2026 `satellite dish system` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "S 333/2004 cl 2 deletes the definitions of 'broadcast television receiver' (and with it the words that excluded a TVRO system) and of 'TVRO system' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:29-31, 48-52), and cl 10 deletes reg 16 'Broadcasting system not to include TVRO system'; the amended text does not say in terms whether a dish system is within it"
-- before the Revised Edition, and after the revocation as the revocation is read
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 28 2 2004 4 11 2026 `television` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "no edition of Rg 1 is deposited for that conduct day as read on that reading day (the earliest deposited text is the Revised Edition 2004, in operation from 29 February 2004)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 1 1 2011 31 10 2012 `television` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "S 548/2012 reg 2(1) revokes Rg 1, deemed in operation on 1 January 2011, first published 31 October 2012; reg 2(2) keeps Rg 1 for licences granted under s 20(1) of the Act for periods before 1 January 2011 (BA1994-S548-2012.txt:28-57): the revoked regulations say nothing about the conduct"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 1 1 2011 30 10 2012 `television` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required to operate a broadcast television receiver in a house or flat: S 333/2004 cl 12(a) deletes reg 27(1) and (2) and substitutes a paragraph (1) that says only 'An application for a licence to install or operate a broadcast television receiver may be made at any post office or at such other places as the Authority may require' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:137-144); reg 27(3) remains ('A licence shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers by the licensee, members of his family and domestic servants resident at the address specified therein', BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), reg 27(4), amended by cl 12(b) to say 'installed or operated by', requires a separate licence for a television installed or operated by a lodger, boarder, resident guest or any person occupying a portion of the premises under a separate tenancy (BA1994-RG1.txt:489-493; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:145-146), and reg 7 now speaks of a contravention of 'section 20 (1) of the Act' alone, cl 6 having deleted 'or of regulation 17, 27 or 36' (BA1994-RG1.txt:264-266; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:92-94)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 31 12 2010 31 10 2012 `television` `in a house or flat` EQUALS "no regulation of the version says in terms that a licence is required to operate a broadcast television receiver in a house or flat: S 333/2004 cl 12(a) deletes reg 27(1) and (2) and substitutes a paragraph (1) that says only 'An application for a licence to install or operate a broadcast television receiver may be made at any post office or at such other places as the Authority may require' (BA1994-S333-2004.txt:137-144); reg 27(3) remains ('A licence shall permit the use of one or more broadcast television receivers and one or more broadcast sound receivers by the licensee, members of his family and domestic servants resident at the address specified therein', BA1994-RG1.txt:485-488), reg 27(4), amended by cl 12(b) to say 'installed or operated by', requires a separate licence for a television installed or operated by a lodger, boarder, resident guest or any person occupying a portion of the premises under a separate tenancy (BA1994-RG1.txt:489-493; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:145-146), and reg 7 now speaks of a contravention of 'section 20 (1) of the Act' alone, cl 6 having deleted 'or of regulation 17, 27 or 36' (BA1994-RG1.txt:264-266; BA1994-S333-2004.txt:92-94)"
#ASSERT `What did the receiver licensing regulations say about a licence for this receiver` 1 1 2011 31 10 2012 `AM radio` `in a vessel that has no ship station licence` EQUALS "S 548/2012 reg 2(1) revokes Rg 1, deemed in operation on 1 January 2011, first published 31 October 2012; reg 2(2) keeps Rg 1 for licences granted under s 20(1) of the Act for periods before 1 January 2011 (BA1994-S548-2012.txt:28-57): the revoked regulations say nothing about the conduct"
